  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Calculate the value of $-\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{7}{10}.$",
  "worked_solution": "We write $-\\frac{2}{5}$ as $-\\frac{4}{10}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{4}{10}-\\frac{7}{10}=\\frac{-4-7}{10}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-4-7$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/d2965f3b03382313757e12920c55ca04be14bf5ae8d5957a15458f5548b8402d.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-4-7}{10}=\\frac{-11}{10}=-\\frac{11}{10}.\n$$",
